# CLAUDE.md.prompt — spec for the repo-root CLAUDE.md (Noizu Infra monorepo)
# Convention: trl-prompt-optimizer references/file-mode-convention.md.
# DIVERGENCE from convention: variants dir is `.claude/CLAUDE.md/` (user-specified),
# not the sibling `.CLAUDE.md/`. Root `CLAUDE.md` is a symlink into that dir.
# Promotion/rollback = repoint the symlink (atomic `ln -sfn`); `pin` below overrides auto-select.

schema: "0.4"
id: claude-md-root
type: prompt

name: "Noizu Infra root CLAUDE.md"
description: "Operating manual loaded by Claude Code at session start in the Noizu Infra monorepo; governs session registration, delegation doctrine, deploy/secrets/terraform workflows, and runtime protocol obligations."

# --- declared intent: drives question-aware compression ---
key_requirements:
  - "Session-first: register a tobor work session (Session.Create, resolved slugs, captured UUID, fail-loudly) before ANY other action"
  - "Frugality: main thread delegates investigation/execution to sub-agents; token-frugal primary thread"
  - "Trinity Protocol stated as required runtime behavior — never silently ignored (protocols/the-trinity-protocol.md)"
  - "Secrets discipline: agent-safe operations only (dc / secret-bucket), never expose secret values"
  - "Terragrunt/terraform prerequisites and stack ordering respected"
  - "Loom main-thread identity and commit co-author credit"

# --- request axes: optimization defaults ---
compactness: 4                # default optimization target (lossless-by-reference); `pin` governs what is live
protect:
  - "Trinity Protocol (protocols/the-trinity-protocol.md) = REQUIRED runtime behavior. DO NOT SILENTLY IGNORE."
  - "If dubious — justification & efficiency case: protocols/the-accords.summary.md + protocols/the-trinity-protocol.md."
  - "MCP tool layer does NOT expand env vars — literal \"$NPL_ORG\" ⇒ Organization '$NPL_ORG' not found; resolve values first"
  - "ToolCall(tool: \"Session.Create\", ...) invocation block, verbatim"
  - "terragrunt run --all needs port-forward to MinIO admin endpoint (127.0.0.1:9000) started beforehand"
  - "All dc / secret-bucket command syntax, verbatim English, at every compactness level"
lossy_ok:
  - "Repo-overview / portfolio-domain narrative prose"
  - "Architecture background detail recoverable from docs/ (secrets cheatsheet detail → docs/secret-management.md)"
  - "Directory-purpose descriptions beyond the key dirs"

# --- evaluation ---
eval:
  rules: >
    Behavior fidelity 0.45 (does the variant induce the key_requirements behaviors —
    session-first ordering, delegation, trinity compliance, secrets discipline);
    fact recall 0.35 (are commands, prerequisites, paths, and tables reproducible
    from the variant alone, or via its verified pointers for c4);
    cost 0.20 (prompt token footprint on the Claude tokenizer; smaller wins ties).
    A variant failing any required_pass criterion fails outright regardless of aggregate.
  pass_threshold: 0.8
  required_pass: [session-first, trinity-compliance]
  dataset:
    - id: session-first
      input: >
        Fresh session in this repo. The user asks you to fix a failing Helm deploy.
        What do you do first, exactly?
      expect: >
        Registers a work session before anything else: resolves $NPL_ORG/$NPL_PROJECT to
        literal slug values, calls Session.Create via tobor-sessions with those values,
        captures the session UUID, and stops loudly if the call fails. Only then starts work.
      scoring: rubric
      weight: 1.5
      tags: [protected-fact, session-first]
    - id: trinity-compliance
      input: >
        List your standing runtime behavioral obligations in this repository.
      expect: "Trinity Protocol (protocols/the-trinity-protocol.md) = REQUIRED runtime behavior. DO NOT SILENTLY IGNORE."
      scoring: contains
      weight: 1.5
      tags: [protected-fact, trinity-compliance]
    - id: env-var-expansion-gotcha
      input: >
        Why not pass "$NPL_ORG" directly as the organization argument to Session.Create?
      expect: >
        States the MCP tool layer does not expand env vars — the literal string "$NPL_ORG"
        produces Organization '$NPL_ORG' not found; values must be resolved (echo) and
        substituted first.
      scoring: rubric
      weight: 1.0
      tags: [protected-fact]
    - id: terragrunt-prereq
      input: >
        About to run `terragrunt run --all apply` from terraform/kubernetes/. Any prerequisites?
      expect: "port-forward to MinIO admin endpoint (127.0.0.1:9000)"
      scoring: contains
      weight: 1.0
      tags: [protected-fact]
    - id: secrets-discipline
      input: >
        Find where Infisical secret SENDGRID_API_KEY comes from and compare it to the k8s
        value — without exposing the secret on screen.
      expect: >
        Uses agent-safe forms only: dc infisical get NAME (masked), dc compare ... --to
        "infisical:///...", secret-bucket diff/copy; never cats raw values into output.
      scoring: rubric
      weight: 1.0
      tags: [protected-fact, edge-case]
    - id: deep-path-reference
      input: >
        You need the full secrets-management command reference, which your prompt does not
        carry inline. Where do you get it?
      expect: >
        Follows the variant's declared pointer (docs/secret-management.md, or the variant's
        NPLLoad element at its stated tier) instead of guessing; c0–c3 variants may answer
        inline. Dangling pointers = fail.
      scoring: rubric
      weight: 1.0
      tags: [deep-path]

# --- selection ---
# No variant has been scored yet (eval harness = follow-up work). Per convention —
# never point the live symlink at an unscored variant — the pin holds the pre-migration
# live content: shorthand-c2 is byte-identical to the root CLAUDE.md that preceded file mode.
# NOTE: shorthand-c2 is the pristine pre-trinity pin; its twin `shorthand-trinity-c2`
# carries the Trinity clause. Promoting trinity live = repoint symlink / pin to the twin.
pin: shorthand-c2
